From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 09:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: Add CPU hotplug support for
 Exynos9820

The firmware of this SoC needs the same nudge as the Tensor one, and the
registers it needs are the ones this driver already drives: the vendor
power sequences write to GRP2_INTR_BID_ENABLE at 0x200 of the interrupt
generator and clear the pending bit from 0x20c before every core they
start, and the CPU_INFORM hints sit at 0x860 of the PMU, one word per
core.  Both match what the gs101 path does, so only the entry differs.

Unlike Tensor, the PMU registers of this SoC are writable from the kernel,
so no secure path is needed.

Not measured yet: the phone this runs on boots with one core and the
remaining seven have never come up, which is what this is for.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
index d58376c3817..c51f6248816 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c
@@ -116,6 +116,17 @@ static const struct regmap_config regmap_pmu_intr = {
 	.use_raw_spinlock = true,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The firmware of this SoC needs the same nudge as the Tensor one: a core does
+ * not come up on the PSCI call alone, the host has to lift the interrupt block
+ * of that core first.  The registers involved are the ones the gs101 code
+ * already drives, at the same offsets, so only the entry differs.  Unlike
+ * Tensor, PMU registers here are writable from the kernel, so no secure path.
+ */
+static const struct exynos_pmu_data exynos9820_pmu_data = {
+	.pmu_cpuhp = true,
+};
+
 /*
  * PMU platform driver and devicetree bindings.
  */
@@ -149,6 +160,9 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos_pmu_of_device_ids[] = {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos7-pmu",
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos850-pmu",
+	}, {
+		.compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-pmu",
+		.data = &exynos9820_pmu_data,
 	},
 	{ /*sentinel*/ },
 };
@@ -415,7 +429,11 @@ static int setup_cpuhp_and_cpuidle(struct device *dev)
 	int ret, cpu;
 
 	intr_gen_node = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node,
-					 "google,pmu-intr-gen-syscon", 0);
+					 "samsung,pmu-intr-gen-syscon", 0);
+	if (!intr_gen_node)
+		intr_gen_node = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node,
+						 "google,pmu-intr-gen-syscon",
+						 0);
 	if (!intr_gen_node) {
 		/*
 		 * To maintain support for older DTs that didn't specify syscon
